  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Architecture studies in the United States exposed Robert Zellinger de Balkany to large regional malls and their integration with suburban housing. Returning to France, he worked with architect Claude Balick on residential schemes at La Celle-Saint-Cloud before combining extensive condominium development with retail and leisure at Parly 2.\n\nThat project became the template for a wider development business. Through SCC, Balkany created or managed centres including Rosny 2, Vélizy 2, Évry 2 and Lyon’s La Part-Dieu. The resulting portfolio ultimately spanned France, Spain, Belgium, Italy, Romania and the Middle East.",
    "html": "<p>Architecture studies in the United States exposed Robert Zellinger de Balkany to large regional malls and their integration with suburban housing. Returning to France, he worked with architect Claude Balick on residential schemes at La Celle-Saint-Cloud before combining extensive condominium development with retail and leisure at Parly 2.</p>\r\n<p>That project became the template for a wider development business. Through SCC, Balkany created or managed centres including Rosny 2, Vélizy 2, Évry 2 and Lyon’s La Part-Dieu. The resulting portfolio ultimately spanned France, Spain, Belgium, Italy, Romania and the Middle East.</p>\r\n",
